#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
Universal Hackintosh Deployment Builder
=======================================

Python 3.12+ / standard-library Tkinter application.

This project is intentionally hardware-neutral. It does not contain a hard-coded
Dell/HP/Lenovo/Apple profile. Instead it gathers a hardware report, turns the
report into a portable SysReport.plist, evaluates broad Hackintosh suitability,
lets the operator customize Intel iGPU/device-property data, downloads the
requested bootloader and kext packages, builds complete EFI directory trees,
and validates/repairs the OpenCore configuration with the matching ocvalidate.

IMPORTANT:
  - A compatibility result is a planning aid, not a guarantee that macOS will boot.
  - Unsupported devices and firmware requirements are reported rather than hidden.
  - Serial/MLB values remain safe placeholders until the operator supplies unique
    values using a trusted SMBIOS-generation workflow.
  - Third-party executable downloads are performed from their official GitHub
    release APIs/assets where possible.
  - Hardware Sniffer produces Report.json; this application converts that report
    to SysReport.plist while preserving the original JSON.

Primary upstream used for hardware collection:
  https://github.com/lzhoang2801/Hardware-Sniffer

The Hardware Sniffer project documents Windows WMI collection, JSON report export,
and ACPI-table dumping; its releases provide Hardware-Sniffer.exe and a CLI build.
This application prefers the CLI for automation and falls back to the GUI/manual
export flow when the CLI cannot complete on the current Windows installation.

The GUI deliberately uses a black terminal-style background with lime text.
"""

